1
00:00:06,690 --> 00:00:08,520
To our victory!

2
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:10,620
Thanks be to our ancestral spirits!

3
00:00:12,860 --> 00:00:17,030
I knew about that ability Frost Pain has.

4
00:00:17,030 --> 00:00:21,160
"Icy Burst," right? I understand
it can only be used three times per day.

5
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:22,540
Pretty well known.

6
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:23,540
Hmph.

7
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:28,150
Heh, yeah, but did you know
that Frost Pain has the power

8
00:00:28,150 --> 00:00:29,880
to protect its user from cold?

9
00:00:30,050 --> 00:00:32,200
It's not without its drawbacks, though.

10
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:38,140
That last ace up his sleeve
he played was that power.

11
00:00:42,310 --> 00:00:44,100
He's an awesome warrior.

12
00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:46,600
Yeah. I'm proud to call him my brother.

13
00:00:52,190 --> 00:00:54,760
Rororo, you did well, too.

14
00:00:56,780 --> 00:00:58,570
What do you think will happen now?

15
00:00:58,570 --> 00:01:01,450
It could be that nothing has ended yet.

16
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:04,750
This "Great One" fellow
might come and attack us now.

17
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:08,040
So, is Zaryusu still asleep?

18
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:10,460
Probably, since he hasn't come out yet.

19
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:14,760
Crusch was pretty exhausted, as well.
We can let them rest for a while.

20
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:17,630
Ho... Well, maybe I'll go peek in on them.

21
00:01:17,630 --> 00:01:21,100
This feast isn't gonna pick up
without its major players here.

22
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:24,100
Don't make too much
of a nuisance of yourself.

23
00:01:46,330 --> 00:01:48,000
Hey, you guys at it?!

24
00:03:28,810 --> 00:03:33,560
Guardians of each floor,
thank you for assembling before me.

25
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:34,730
We'll start with you, Victim.

26
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:41,110
This is your first time
meeting everyone else, isn't it?

27
00:03:44,990 --> 00:03:47,120
Pleasure to meet all of you.

28
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:49,120
I am Victim.

29
00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:53,750
I've called you, the guardian of
the eighth floor, for one reason--

30
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:57,380
we still have not identified
the foe who went after Shalltear.

31
00:03:57,380 --> 00:04:01,260
We must consider that an as-yet
unforeseen incident may occur.

32
00:04:01,420 --> 00:04:05,720
As such, we require a powerful skill
that is invoked by your death

33
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:09,820
to protect all of the guardians,
myself included.

34
00:04:10,350 --> 00:04:14,310
I am sorry. I promise
to bring you back to life right away,

35
00:04:14,310 --> 00:04:15,520
so I hope you'll forgive me.

36
00:04:15,850 --> 00:04:21,110
Do not let it bother you, Lord Ains.
I was born in order to die.

37
00:04:21,110 --> 00:04:25,030
If that power will be
of assistance to the Supreme One,

38
00:04:25,030 --> 00:04:27,530
nothing could give me more joy.

39
00:04:27,660 --> 00:04:32,830
One of the catchphrases
that Nazarick used goes like this--

40
00:04:32,830 --> 00:04:36,330
"Greater love hath no man than this,

41
00:04:36,330 --> 00:04:40,300
that he lay down his life for his friends."

42
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:43,300
It is truly an expression
that fits you perfectly.

43
00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:45,550
I am grateful for your love.

44
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:47,800
Your words are more than I deserve.

45
00:04:48,430 --> 00:04:49,930
Next up, Demiurge.

46
00:04:49,930 --> 00:04:50,680
My lord?

47
00:04:50,930 --> 00:04:55,270
First, allow me to honor you
for always answering my call.

48
00:04:55,440 --> 00:04:58,150
What are you saying?
It is only to be expected

49
00:04:58,150 --> 00:05:00,550
that I should report to you
at once when you call, Lord Ains.

50
00:05:01,030 --> 00:05:05,490
Yes. It is evident that the sheepskin
parchment that you brought

51
00:05:05,490 --> 00:05:09,340
can stand up to use in lower-tier scrolls.

52
00:05:09,870 --> 00:05:12,160
Can I count on a stable supply of it?

53
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:14,710
Yes. That will not be a problem.

54
00:05:14,710 --> 00:05:17,170
I have acquired an ample number of them.

55
00:05:17,170 --> 00:05:21,800
I see. So, what was the name
of these beasts, again?

56
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,300
Beasts? Ah...

57
00:05:24,670 --> 00:05:26,680
As they are two-legged sheep
from the holy kingdom,

58
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:30,300
how does the name "Abelion Sheep" sound?

59
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:32,480
Indeed. Sheep, huh?

60
00:05:32,890 --> 00:05:36,980
So the beasts are actually chimeras--
or rather, a subspecies.

61
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:40,060
In Yggdrasil, chimeras had
the heads of a lion and a goat,

62
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:42,400
and their tails were snakes.
He must be trying to indicate

63
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:44,890
that a beast with a sheep mixed in
is something different.

64
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:50,320
I think goats would be better, but very well.
Continue what you are doing.

65
00:05:51,580 --> 00:05:52,990
Now, as for you, Shalltear...

66
00:05:52,990 --> 00:05:54,200
Y-Yes?

67
00:05:54,370 --> 00:05:57,080
Regarding the splinter 
you have in your soul...

68
00:05:57,080 --> 00:06:00,960
Ah, Lord Ains, after being appointed
to the position of guardian,

69
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:02,750
and then doing what I did,

70
00:06:02,750 --> 00:06:04,670
I ask you to please give me a punishment

71
00:06:04,670 --> 00:06:06,340
worthy of a reprehensible fool
such as myself!

72
00:06:07,050 --> 00:06:10,370
All right. I will settle on one later
and give it to you.

73
00:06:11,430 --> 00:06:12,930
Lastly, Cocytus...

74
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:17,430
You ended in defeat.

75
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:22,690
Yes, my lord. I am terribly sorry
for my offense. I was--

76
00:06:22,690 --> 00:06:26,190
Cocytus! If you're going to apologize,
lift up your face!

77
00:06:26,190 --> 00:06:27,740
I beg your pardon.

78
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:31,200
Cocytus, tell me the reason
why you were beaten.

79
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:35,700
Right. I am very sorry for
losing the army you entrusted to me.

80
00:06:35,700 --> 00:06:36,700
Not that.

81
00:06:37,290 --> 00:06:39,000
Let me state upfront

82
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:42,840
that I don't intend to come down
on you too hard for this defeat.

83
00:06:47,090 --> 00:06:51,510
The reason being that I don't care
who you are, everyone makes mistakes.

84
00:06:51,510 --> 00:06:53,700
That goes for me, as well.

85
00:06:54,970 --> 00:06:59,980
That being said, I ask you, Cocytus,
how could you have won?

86
00:07:02,230 --> 00:07:07,360
I underestimated the Lizard Men.
I should have acted more cautiously.

87
00:07:07,530 --> 00:07:09,400
Mm-hmm, that is correct.

88
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:12,740
You must never underestimate someone,
no matter how weak they are.

89
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:14,120
Is there anything else?

90
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:17,790
Yes. I think I may have had
insufficient information.

91
00:07:17,790 --> 00:07:20,040
The enemy's strength, the topography--

92
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:22,540
I have learned that without
making sure of such considerations,

93
00:07:22,540 --> 00:07:25,960
the chances of my victory were lowered,
no matter what I did.

94
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:26,740
Mm-hmm.

95
00:07:28,630 --> 00:07:30,970
Not having enough commanders
was also a problem.

96
00:07:31,380 --> 00:07:33,590
Since they were all lower-level undead,

97
00:07:33,590 --> 00:07:37,470
I should have put in place
those who could issue orders as necessary.

98
00:07:37,620 --> 00:07:38,850
Anything besides that?

99
00:07:38,850 --> 00:07:43,350
I apologize, but that is
all I can think of right now.

100
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:45,230
Outstanding!

101
00:07:45,230 --> 00:07:49,120
Except for that Elder Lich,
they were all spawn undead.

102
00:07:49,780 --> 00:07:53,990
Their demise has absolutely
no effect on Nazarick.

103
00:07:53,990 --> 00:07:56,760
Considering what one of
my guardians has learned from this,

104
00:07:56,760 --> 00:07:58,410
I will be getting change back from this deal.

105
00:07:58,410 --> 00:08:00,750
Thank you very much, Lord Ains.

106
00:08:00,750 --> 00:08:01,750
Be that as it may,

107
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:05,710
the fact remains that you lost,
and you must be punished.

108
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:12,260
Cocytus! You will personally
mop up that sludge!

109
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:14,550
Exterminate the Lizard Men!

110
00:08:15,090 --> 00:08:18,100
This time, without relying on anyone else.

111
00:08:20,140 --> 00:08:25,190
A fantastic idea! Cocytus will expunge
his sin of being defeated,

112
00:08:25,190 --> 00:08:27,520
along with all of the Lizard Men!

113
00:08:28,190 --> 00:08:29,660
Lord Ains...

114
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:33,280
I have a request I would like to make.

115
00:08:33,950 --> 00:08:35,780
I beg of you, Lord Ains...

116
00:08:37,070 --> 00:08:40,410
You, who have brought defeat
to glorious Nazarick,

117
00:08:40,410 --> 00:08:44,670
dare to petition Lord Ains?!
Remember where your place is!

118
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:48,670
--Cocytus--
--It's all right, Albedo.

119
00:08:49,630 --> 00:08:56,180
Would you lift up your face, Cocytus,
and tell me what your request is?

120
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:03,320
Well, Cocytus? I simply
want to know what you're thinking,

121
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:05,690
and what you would like to say.

122
00:09:06,020 --> 00:09:11,320
I am against killing all of the Lizard Men.
I beg you, show them mercy.

123
00:09:11,650 --> 00:09:15,530
Cocytus, do you realize what you're saying?!

124
00:09:15,530 --> 00:09:18,280
Albedo, do not get in the middle of this.

125
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:20,580
I beg your pardon. Please forgive me.

126
00:09:20,830 --> 00:09:26,080
Now then, Cocytus, you must have
a pretty good reason for your request.

127
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:30,040
Something that will benefit
the Great Tomb of Nazarick.

128
00:09:30,040 --> 00:09:31,710
Tell me what that is.

129
00:09:31,710 --> 00:09:32,590
Yes, my lord.

130
00:09:32,590 --> 00:09:37,510
There is a chance that valiant warriors
will appear among their number.

131
00:09:37,510 --> 00:09:39,760
In my judgment,
it will be more beneficial to us

132
00:09:39,760 --> 00:09:42,420
to have the Lizard Men
pledge loyalty to Nazarick,

133
00:09:42,420 --> 00:09:44,350
and make them our subordinates.

134
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:46,910
That is indeed a convincing proposal.

135
00:09:47,440 --> 00:09:51,270
If we were to use the Lizard Man
corpses to create undead,

136
00:09:51,270 --> 00:09:54,990
they would only be of about the same level
as those from human corpses.

137
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:59,450
As such, there is no reason
to insist on Lizard Man corpses.

138
00:09:59,450 --> 00:10:00,490
In that case...

139
00:10:00,490 --> 00:10:03,910
However! It would be more cost-effective
to use undead created by me

140
00:10:03,910 --> 00:10:08,500
than it would be
to leave the Lizard Men alive.

141
00:10:09,460 --> 00:10:13,300
If there are any other benefits,
I'd like to hear them.

142
00:10:13,300 --> 00:10:16,070
--Well, I...
--How about it, Cocytus?

143
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:21,350
If you have nothing more, than you won't
mind exterminating then, yes?

144
00:10:22,970 --> 00:10:24,720
I see. That's too bad.

145
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:26,020
Lord Ains?

146
00:10:26,390 --> 00:10:27,890
What is it, Demiurge?

147
00:10:27,890 --> 00:10:28,540
My lord,

148
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:33,400
what if we were to use the Lizard Men
in a governability experiment?

149
00:10:33,610 --> 00:10:36,150
Ho, now this sounds like
an interesting idea.

150
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:38,840
Yes. The time will likely come

151
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:41,120
when we will be handling
different races and powers.

152
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:44,700
I humbly submit that we ought to
perform an experiment in governing

153
00:10:44,700 --> 00:10:48,290
in which we rule the Lizard Men's villages
by means other than fear

154
00:10:48,290 --> 00:10:49,670
for when that time comes.

155
00:10:50,620 --> 00:10:53,170
A terrific suggestion, Demiurge!

156
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:54,670
Thank you very much.

157
00:10:55,590 --> 00:10:58,170
We will then accept Demiurge's proposal,

158
00:10:58,170 --> 00:11:02,180
and shift from exterminating
the Lizard Men to occupying them.

159
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:02,930
Yes, my lord!

160
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:05,810
Demiurge, I'm impressed.

161
00:11:06,180 --> 00:11:08,560
How can you say that, Lord Ains?

162
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:12,730
I am sure that you were already
aware of my modest proposal.

163
00:11:12,730 --> 00:11:15,190
You were simply waiting
for Cocytus, were you not?

164
00:11:15,650 --> 00:11:20,820
Hmph, you give me
too much credit. All I wanted...

165
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:26,200
...was for him to display some of his own
thinking, regardless of what it was.

166
00:11:26,580 --> 00:11:28,220
Listen to me, guardians!

167
00:11:28,830 --> 00:11:33,350
Orders are not things for you
to blindly obey and carry out.

168
00:11:33,880 --> 00:11:37,050
You must mull them over
a little bit before you act!

169
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:41,970
Consider what will lead to
the greatest benefit for Nazarick!

170
00:11:42,050 --> 00:11:43,040
Yes, my lord!

171
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:48,430
Now then, Cocytus, consequently,
your punishment must now be changed.

172
00:11:48,430 --> 00:11:51,020
You will govern the Lizard Men,

173
00:11:51,020 --> 00:11:53,480
and instill loyalty
toward Nazarick within them.

174
00:11:53,850 --> 00:11:56,230
Rule through fear is forbidden.

175
00:11:56,400 --> 00:11:57,980
As you wish.

176
00:11:58,780 --> 00:12:01,820
I, Cocytus, promise to work hard enough

177
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:05,620
to measure up to the great mercy
you have shown me, Lord Ains.

178
00:12:05,990 --> 00:12:08,780
All right, guardians,
I order you all to move out.

179
00:12:09,370 --> 00:12:15,880
One team as a decoy, and another
to flaunt our power to the Lizard Men.

180
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:20,670
Albedo, make ready our soldiers.
Activate Gargantua, as well.

181
00:12:20,670 --> 00:12:22,130
As you command.

182
00:12:22,130 --> 00:12:23,670
Can I also assume that by sending a decoy,

183
00:12:23,670 --> 00:12:26,570
you are considering that there is
someone who enjoys peeking at us,

184
00:12:26,570 --> 00:12:31,140
and are giving the wrong impression
as to our true intentions?

185
00:12:31,140 --> 00:12:32,480
That is correct.

186
00:12:32,480 --> 00:12:33,890
Very good.

187
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:37,690
All right, everyone, time to get moving!

188
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:41,990
I'm grateful to you, Demiurge.

189
00:12:41,990 --> 00:12:44,490
There's no need for that, Cocytus.

190
00:12:44,490 --> 00:12:48,780
For you see, this is probably
the outcome that Lord Ains desired.

191
00:12:48,780 --> 00:12:49,410
Huh?

192
00:12:49,410 --> 00:12:53,410
You're saying that everything
is going according to Lord Ains' plan?

193
00:12:53,410 --> 00:12:55,290
Leave it to Lord Ains!

194
00:12:55,290 --> 00:13:00,670
B-But then, um, I mean, I'm just saying,

195
00:13:00,670 --> 00:13:04,550
did he assume ahead of time
that Cocytus would lose?

196
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:06,710
Not so much lose, perhaps,

197
00:13:06,710 --> 00:13:09,460
as he may have been entertaining 
the idea that Cocytus would

198
00:13:09,460 --> 00:13:10,760
probe the Lizard Men's strength,

199
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:13,060
and recommend whether or not
they could beat them.

200
00:13:13,060 --> 00:13:16,900
That's Lord Ains for you!
He truly is beyond incredible!

201
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:20,320
It's fair to say that his assumption

202
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:23,670
of the role of coordinator for
the Supreme Ones was not just for show!

203
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:44,380
Wow, that was amazing! I didn't expect
Cocytus to say what he did.

204
00:13:44,380 --> 00:13:46,820
In Yggdrasil, if you do anything
you don't have the skills for,

205
00:13:46,820 --> 00:13:48,260
it's sure to end in failure.

206
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:51,970
But if he can gain tactics
and strategies from this experience,

207
00:13:51,970 --> 00:13:55,480
that goes to prove that
we have the potential to grow.

208
00:13:56,060 --> 00:13:59,020
But growth means change.

209
00:13:59,020 --> 00:14:03,780
I can't even say that the absolute loyalty
of the guardians will never change.

210
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:05,680
Ah! That's scary stuff!

211
00:14:06,070 --> 00:14:10,070
I wonder if there's anyone around
who can teach me kingcraft.

212
00:14:10,870 --> 00:14:14,810
Now, it's about time
I got ready to move out.

213
00:14:15,910 --> 00:14:16,560
Hmm?

214
00:14:21,670 --> 00:14:26,590
There's a floral scent.
Have they sprinkled perfume on the bed?

215
00:14:26,590 --> 00:14:29,720
Is this what wealthy people's beds are like?

216
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:35,430
If so, maybe I should keep that in mind
when pretending to be rich.

217
00:14:36,850 --> 00:14:38,690
I had anticipated this,

218
00:14:39,350 --> 00:14:40,560
but this is too soon.

219
00:14:41,020 --> 00:14:43,070
Huh? It can't be.

220
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:45,270
I-Impossible.

221
00:14:45,650 --> 00:14:50,320
Have you noticed it, too?
That is all magic equipment.

222
00:14:50,490 --> 00:14:52,340
A mythical army.

223
00:14:56,330 --> 00:14:58,550
What's with this cold wind?

224
00:14:58,910 --> 00:15:00,170
This isn't possible.

225
00:15:01,830 --> 00:15:04,670
The only thing that can
produce wind like this

226
00:15:04,670 --> 00:15:07,970
is sixth tier magic or better--
"Control Weather."

227
00:15:07,970 --> 00:15:09,410
Sixth tier?

228
00:15:10,880 --> 00:15:14,930
This is the power
of the so-called "Great One"?

229
00:15:15,140 --> 00:15:16,270
Remain calm!

230
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:19,910
Do not be intimidated, warriors!

231
00:15:21,810 --> 00:15:23,440
Refrain from any actions

232
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:27,320
that would disappoint
the many ancestral spirits behind you!

233
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:30,100
What do you think?

234
00:15:30,950 --> 00:15:32,320
They're making a move,

235
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:35,580
but they don't appear
to be preparing for battle.

236
00:15:36,910 --> 00:15:38,580
What are they planning to do?

237
00:15:39,540 --> 00:15:40,580
Hmm...

238
00:15:49,670 --> 00:15:51,980
Is this the ruler of death?

239
00:15:57,850 --> 00:15:59,310
What is that, exactly?

240
00:15:59,310 --> 00:16:02,020
I don't know. I don't know what that is.

241
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:14,570
Everyone, hurry and get to higher ground!

242
00:16:22,830 --> 00:16:27,210
We can be sure this is
the "Great One," all right.

243
00:16:27,210 --> 00:16:28,260
Most likely.

244
00:16:28,630 --> 00:16:34,930
I'm sold. From where that monster stands,
we might as well be dung.

245
00:16:34,930 --> 00:16:35,640
Hmm?

246
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:37,360
What is that?

247
00:16:38,970 --> 00:16:40,090
What is that thing?!

248
00:17:19,930 --> 00:17:21,040
It can't be...

249
00:17:31,980 --> 00:17:34,360
A royal procession?

250
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:06,810
We bring you the words of the Great One.

251
00:18:06,810 --> 00:18:09,900
The Great One wishes to converse with you.

252
00:18:09,900 --> 00:18:13,190
Let your delegate step forward at once.

253
00:18:13,190 --> 00:18:19,740
Know that time that is wasted
is displeasing to the Great One.

254
00:18:25,080 --> 00:18:30,270
H-He used all those monsters
simply for <i>that</i>?

255
00:18:31,290 --> 00:18:32,260
Zaryusu...

256
00:18:34,090 --> 00:18:35,010
My brother...

257
00:18:36,090 --> 00:18:37,360
...will you come with me?

258
00:18:38,090 --> 00:18:38,800
Mm-hmm.

259
00:18:42,550 --> 00:18:43,760
Zaryusu...

260
00:18:43,760 --> 00:18:44,640
Crusch,

261
00:18:44,890 --> 00:18:45,630
I'll be back.

262
00:18:46,230 --> 00:18:47,290
Be careful.

263
00:18:55,610 --> 00:18:56,860
Thanks.

264
00:18:56,860 --> 00:18:58,990
Considering their numbers,

265
00:18:58,990 --> 00:19:01,950
they may think you going alone
to be disrespectful, Brother.

266
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:06,910
Besides, if we are killed
to make an example, I, as a traveler,

267
00:19:06,910 --> 00:19:09,460
will not be missed in regard
to the unity of the tribes.

268
00:19:11,880 --> 00:19:15,300
I am the representative
of the Lizard Men, Shasuryu Shasha!

269
00:19:15,300 --> 00:19:18,720
And this is the mightiest
of the Lizard Men...

270
00:19:19,050 --> 00:19:20,640
...Zaryusu Shasha!

271
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:28,140
Our master does not feel that
your posture is conducive to listening.

272
00:19:28,140 --> 00:19:29,340
Demiurge?

273
00:19:30,520 --> 00:19:31,730
Prostrate yourselves!

274
00:19:34,690 --> 00:19:36,230
Do not resist!

275
00:19:38,820 --> 00:19:41,860
Lord Ains, they have
adopted a listening posture.

276
00:19:41,860 --> 00:19:44,240
Good work. Lift up their heads.

277
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:46,740
You are permitted to lift your heads!

278
00:19:48,370 --> 00:19:53,710
I am the master of the Great Tomb
of Nazarick, Ains Ooal Gown.

279
00:19:53,710 --> 00:19:58,510
First, I express my gratitude to you
for assisting with my experiment.

280
00:19:59,970 --> 00:20:01,830
Now, onto the main subject.

281
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:05,080
You will fall under my rule.

282
00:20:05,510 --> 00:20:06,310
Wha--?

283
00:20:06,310 --> 00:20:08,350
However, it is likely...

284
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:10,930
...that you do not wish
to come under the rule of someone

285
00:20:10,930 --> 00:20:13,420
against whom you have achieved victory.

286
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:17,710
Thus, in four hours, I will attack again.

287
00:20:18,610 --> 00:20:23,610
The attacker will be one of
my trusted aides, Cocytus, on his own.

288
00:20:23,610 --> 00:20:27,490
If you are able
to prevail against him, as well,

289
00:20:27,490 --> 00:20:31,620
I promise to henceforth
leave you completely alone.

290
00:20:32,620 --> 00:20:33,620
We surrender--

291
00:20:33,960 --> 00:20:37,800
I would prefer you
not suggest something as tedious

292
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:39,630
as to surrender without fighting!

293
00:20:39,630 --> 00:20:41,260
You're making an example of us?

294
00:20:41,260 --> 00:20:47,010
I am done speaking. You have four hours.
Enjoy them while you can.

295
00:20:47,140 --> 00:20:50,430
I ask that you wait! Will this ice melt?

296
00:20:50,430 --> 00:20:52,430
Ah, that's right.

297
00:20:52,640 --> 00:20:55,810
I simply did not want to
dirty myself with your mud.

298
00:20:55,810 --> 00:20:59,070
I will dispel the effect of the magic later.

299
00:21:00,230 --> 00:21:03,200
Farwell then, Lizard Men. Gate!

300
00:21:04,280 --> 00:21:06,500
Goodbye, Lizard Men.

301
00:21:07,740 --> 00:21:09,080
See you!

302
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:10,700
This is goodbye.

303
00:21:10,700 --> 00:21:14,290
Um, er... well, please take care.

304
00:21:14,290 --> 00:21:16,090
I bid you farewell.

305
00:21:17,330 --> 00:21:19,090
You are free to move.

306
00:21:19,290 --> 00:21:23,050
Do try to enjoy yourselves, Lizard Men.

307
00:21:26,050 --> 00:21:28,010
Damn them!

308
00:21:29,510 --> 00:21:31,970
This amounts to a ritual 
sacrifice, doesn't it?

309
00:21:32,220 --> 00:21:33,980
So, what do we do?

310
00:21:33,980 --> 00:21:37,650
Call all of the warrior class
Lizard Men to arms.

311
00:21:37,650 --> 00:21:39,440
In addition, we have those of us here--

312
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:42,390
Could I ask that it just be five of us?

313
00:21:42,860 --> 00:21:43,740
Hmm?

314
00:21:43,740 --> 00:21:48,410
If their goal is to demonstrate
their overwhelming power,

315
00:21:48,410 --> 00:21:51,410
they are unlikely to kill us all.
If that's the case,

316
00:21:51,410 --> 00:21:55,040
we will need a central figure
for the survivors to organize around.

317
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:56,420
A sound argument.

318
00:21:56,420 --> 00:21:59,130
Mm-hmm. However, Zaryusu...

319
00:21:59,130 --> 00:22:01,960
Why not? I agree with him.

320
00:22:02,250 --> 00:22:05,470
Then that's what we'll do.
Crusch would be suitable.

321
00:22:05,470 --> 00:22:06,720
Just a minute!

322
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:08,430
I'm going to fight, too!

323
00:22:08,430 --> 00:22:11,350
Zaryusu, why would you
say such a thing at this point?

324
00:22:11,560 --> 00:22:14,350
Because we've been given
a chance to survive.

325
00:22:15,060 --> 00:22:16,270
Don't give me that!

326
00:22:18,060 --> 00:22:20,670
Zaryusu, you convince her.

327
00:22:21,070 --> 00:22:22,960
I'll see you again in four hours.

328
00:22:35,910 --> 00:22:38,500
Crusch, please understand.

329
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:42,590
There's no way I can understand!
Besides, there's no guarantee we'll lose!

330
00:22:42,590 --> 00:22:46,010
With my priestly powers, we might win!

331
00:22:46,840 --> 00:22:49,640
I don't want to let
the female I'm in love with die.

332
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:55,890
Please grant the wish of this foolish male.

333
00:22:59,940 --> 00:23:01,120
That's not fair...

334
00:23:02,820 --> 00:23:03,740
I'm sorry.

335
00:23:05,530 --> 00:23:08,280
You'll probably be killed.

336
00:23:08,280 --> 00:23:11,320
--Yeah.
--And you're asking me to watch you die?

337
00:23:12,030 --> 00:23:14,350
After we've become
so attached to each other?

338
00:23:14,910 --> 00:23:15,600
Yeah.

339
00:23:16,750 --> 00:23:19,160
I'm so happy that we met each other...

340
00:23:19,460 --> 00:23:21,240
...but also, so sad.

341
00:23:37,890 --> 00:23:39,110
Impregnate me!

342
00:23:39,110 --> 00:23:41,110


